1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,733
Across aquaculture farms, multiple ponds depend on electricity to keep aerators running.

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:14,600
When the power fails, the farmer must decide which ponds receive limited backup electricity.

3
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:19,700
Introducing AquaResQ,

4
00:00:19,833 --> 00:00:23,733
Team SKAY's explainable emergency intelligence and resource optimization system.

5
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:34,833
Each pond has its own planning profile, including water depth,

6
00:00:34,967 --> 00:00:38,000
starting oxygen, shrimp biomass and aerator requirements.

7
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:49,267
The outage simulator estimates how dissolved oxygen may change over time.

8
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:52,000
Its oxygen-balance model produces trajectories that

9
00:00:52,133 --> 00:00:55,600
can be compared against a chosen protection threshold.

10
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:06,400
In our critical scenario, three aerators need six kilowatts,

11
00:01:06,533 --> 00:01:09,133
but the generator supplies only four.

12
00:01:09,267 --> 00:01:13,600
Over twelve hours, available energy is limited to forty-eight kilowatt-hours.

13
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:23,100
AquaResQ evaluates feasible whole-pond aerator allocations,

14
00:01:23,233 --> 00:01:25,833
checking generator power and available energy.

15
00:01:25,967 --> 00:01:30,733
It selects the combination that minimizes the modeled integrated oxygen deficit.

16
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:48,767
In this simulated example, AquaResQ reduces integrated oxygen deficit from eighty-nine point two eight to twenty-three point six —

17
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:51,933
approximately seventy-four percent below the no-generator case.

18
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:00,233
Every recommendation is explainable.

19
00:02:00,367 --> 00:02:05,133
The system shows which ponds receive power, why alternatives were excluded,

20
00:02:05,267 --> 00:02:08,300
and the trade-offs between different allocation strategies.

21
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:18,533
Today, AquaResQ is a simulated planning prototype.

22
00:02:18,667 --> 00:02:21,700
Expert review and field validation come next.

23
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:24,700
AquaResQ.

24
00:02:24,833 --> 00:02:26,567
When every pond counts.

